      "content": "The problem is the internal report specifically says the margin dip won't be \"temporary\"—it says the cumulative impact over three years will be a permanent 12% reduction in free cash flow. If Vance digs into the three-year projection and sees those numbers, we're done. Is there any way to interpret that data so it doesn't look like a permanent hit? Or should we just tell him the report's methodology is flawed? I need to know if I can honestly tell him the impact is manageable without him smelling a rat.",
